        "title": "19th-Century Analysis - Cauchy, Riemann, Weierstrass, Cantor, Dedekind",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "What Cauchy found wrong:\n  Fourier (1822): The heat equation's solution requires\n  \"any function\" to have a Fourier series.\n  But what IS a function? Can any arbitrary rule be a function?"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-19TH-CENTURY-ANALYSIS.md#005",
      "path": [
